# TRACE-BASED DISCOVERY
# Use execution traces to discover loop structure

"" println
"╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗" println
"║  TRACE-BASED PROGRAM DISCOVERY                           ║" println
"║  Using execution traces to find loop patterns            ║" println
"╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝" println
"" println

# The key insight:
# We can STEP through a fiber and observe the stack at each step.
# This gives us a TRACE - a sequence of states.
#
# For factorial(4):
#   Stack trace: [4] → [1,4] → [4,1,4] → [4,4] → [4,3] → ...
#
# The trace reveals the STRUCTURE of the computation:
#   - What gets duplicated
#   - What gets multiplied
#   - How the counter changes
#
# If we have traces for multiple inputs, we can find COMMON PATTERNS.

"=== Collecting Execution Traces ===" println
"" println

# Manual factorial for reference
[ 1 swap [ dup 0 eq not ] [ dup rot mul swap 1 sub ] while drop ] "fact" def

# Step through and collect stack states
# ( quote n max-steps -- trace-list )
[
  "max" swap mem-set
  "n" swap mem-set
  "code" swap mem-set
  
  # Create fiber and inject n
  "code" mem-get fiber-new "n" mem-get fiber-inject
  "fiber" swap mem-set
  
  # Collect trace
  "trace" 0 list mem-set
  "steps" 0 mem-set
  
  [
    "fiber" mem-get fiber-status "done" eq not
    "steps" mem-get "max" mem-get lt
    and
  ] [
    # Record current stack
    "trace" mem-get
    "fiber" mem-get fiber-stack
    list-push
    "trace" swap mem-set
    
    # Step
    "fiber" mem-get fiber-step "fiber" swap mem-set
    "steps" mem-get 1 add "steps" swap mem-set
  ] while
  
  # Record final stack
  "trace" mem-get
  "fiber" mem-get fiber-stack
  list-push
  "trace" swap mem-set
  
  "trace" mem-get
] "collect-trace" def

# Show a trace
"Trace of factorial(3):" println
[ 1 swap [ dup 0 eq not ] [ dup rot mul swap 1 sub ] while drop ] 3 50 collect-trace
"trace3" swap mem-set

"trace3" mem-get 
[ "  " print to-text println ] each

"" println
"Trace of factorial(4):" println
[ 1 swap [ dup 0 eq not ] [ dup rot mul swap 1 sub ] while drop ] 4 50 collect-trace
"trace4" swap mem-set

"trace4" mem-get 
[ "  " print to-text println ] each

"" println
"=== Analyzing Traces ===" println
"" println

# What patterns can we see?
# 
# For factorial, the trace shows:
# [n] → [1, n] → ... → [result]
#
# The "loop body" appears as a REPEATING SUBSEQUENCE in the trace.
# 
# Key observation: 
# Between iterations, the stack has form [acc, counter]
# Each iteration: counter decrements, acc *= counter

"Looking at stack transitions..." println
"" println

# Extract just the 2-element stacks (the loop state)
"Loop states from factorial(4):" println
"trace4" mem-get
[
  dup list-len 2 eq [
    "  " print to-text println
  ] [ drop ] if
] each

"" println
"=== The Discovery Insight ===" println
"" println

"From the trace, we can see:" println
"" println
"  [1, 4] → ... → [4, 3] → ... → [12, 2] → ... → [24, 1] → ... → [24, 0]" println
"" println
"Pattern:" println
"  - Second element decreases by 1 each iteration" println
"  - First element = previous first × previous second" println
"" println
"This IS the loop body: acc' = acc × counter, counter' = counter - 1" println
"" println

"=== Trace Diffing ===" println
"" println

# Compare traces for n=3 and n=4
# The DIFFERENCE tells us what the loop does

"Comparing final stacks:" println
"  fact(3) ends with: " print "trace3" mem-get dup list-len 1 sub list-get to-text println
"  fact(4) ends with: " print "trace4" mem-get dup list-len 1 sub list-get to-text println
"" println

"Comparing trace lengths:" println
"  fact(3) trace: " print "trace3" mem-get list-len to-text print " steps" println
"  fact(4) trace: " print "trace4" mem-get list-len to-text print " steps" println
"" println

"Observation: fact(4) has more steps than fact(3)" println
"The DIFFERENCE in step count reveals the loop iteration count!" println

"" println
"=== Towards Automatic Discovery ===" println
"" println

"Strategy:" println
"1. Run unknown function on multiple inputs" println
"2. Collect execution traces" println
"3. Find REPEATING patterns in each trace (loop body candidates)" println
"4. Find COMMON patterns across traces (the actual loop body)" println
"5. Synthesize: init + while(cond, body)" println
"" println

# Let's try to find the repeating pattern automatically
"=== Finding Repeating Stack Patterns ===" println
"" println

# For factorial, the pattern is:
# Stack goes [a, n] → [a', n-1] where a' = a*n
# 
# We look for "similar shaped" stacks that differ predictably

"Looking for [acc, counter] patterns where counter decrements..." println
"" println

# Check trace4 for 2-element stacks
"prev-acc" 0 mem-set
"prev-cnt" 0 mem-set
"found-pattern" 0 mem-set

"trace4" mem-get
[
  dup list-len 2 eq [
    # This is a 2-element stack [acc, cnt]
    dup 0 list-get "curr-acc" swap mem-set
    dup 1 list-get "curr-cnt" swap mem-set
    
    # Check if counter decremented from previous
    "prev-cnt" mem-get 0 eq not [
      "curr-cnt" mem-get "prev-cnt" mem-get 1 sub eq [
        # Counter decremented!
        # Check if acc *= prev-counter
        "curr-acc" mem-get "prev-acc" mem-get "prev-cnt" mem-get mul eq [
          "  Transition: [" print 
          "prev-acc" mem-get to-text print ", " print
          "prev-cnt" mem-get to-text print "] → [" print
          "curr-acc" mem-get to-text print ", " print
          "curr-cnt" mem-get to-text print "]" println
          "    Pattern: acc × cnt, cnt - 1" println
          "found-pattern" mem-get 1 add "found-pattern" swap mem-set
        ] [ ] if
      ] [ ] if
    ] [ ] if
    
    # Update previous
    "curr-acc" mem-get "prev-acc" swap mem-set
    "curr-cnt" mem-get "prev-cnt" swap mem-set
    
    drop
  ] [ drop ] if
] each

"" println
"Found " print "found-pattern" mem-get to-text print " instances of the pattern!" println

"" println
"╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗" println
"║  INSIGHT                                                 ║" println
"║                                                          ║" println
"║  By analyzing TRACES, we discovered:                     ║" println
"║    • Loop state: [accumulator, counter]                  ║" println
"║    • Transition: acc' = acc × cnt, cnt' = cnt - 1        ║" println
"║    • Termination: when cnt = 0                           ║" println
"║                                                          ║" println
"║  This IS factorial's loop body - found from traces!      ║" println
"║                                                          ║" println
"║  The trace reveals structure that outputs alone hide.    ║" println
"╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝" println
